(DISSOLUTION OF MUSLIM MARRIAGES ACT, 1939) '
(Act No. 8 of 1939 Published in Gazette of India on 17 March 1939) '
(Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice, Government of India) '
(Repository: India Code indiacode.nic.in / Indian Kanoon doc 110749554) '
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) '
(An Act to consolidate and clarify the provisions of Muslim law relating to suits) '
(for dissolution of marriage by women married under Muslim law.) '
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) '
(Section 1: Short title and extent - Extends to the whole of India.) '
(Section 2: Grounds for decree for dissolution of marriage:) '
(  i Husband whereabouts unknown for 4 years decree effective after 6 months;) '
(  ii Husband neglected or failed to provide maintenance for 2 years;) '
(  iii Husband sentenced to imprisonment for 7 years or upwards;) '
(  iv Husband failed to perform marital obligations for 3 years without cause;) '
(  v Husband impotent at marriage and continues to be so 1 year medical proviso;) '
(  vi Husband insane for 2 years or suffering from leprosy or virulent venereal disease;) '
(  vii Option of puberty: Repudiated marriage before 18 if married before 15 unconsummated;) '
(  viii Cruelty: Physical assault, infamous life, forcing immoral life, disposing property,) '
(         obstructing religious profession, or inequitable treatment among multiple wives;) '
(  ix Any other ground recognized as valid for dissolution of marriage under Muslim law.) '
(Section 3: Notice to be served on heirs of husband when whereabouts unknown.) '
(Section 4: Effect of conversion to another faith - Renunciation of Islam by wife does) '
(           not dissolve marriage automatically, but preserves right to decree under Section 2.) '
(Section 5: Right to dower Mahr not affected - Wife retains full entitlement to Mahr.) '
(Section 6: Repeal of Section 5 of Act 26 of 1937.) '
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) '
